{title: When I See the Blood}
{subtitle: Exodus 12:1–42}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Down in the land of Egypt where the bricks were made with tears
The [Abmaj7]people cried for [Eb]freedom for four hundred years
[Ab]Then Moses said, [Eb]get ready now, put [Eb/G]your sandals on [Ab]your feet
Take [Eb]a lamb for every household and [Bb]the bread without the [Eb]yeast
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
When I see the blood, I will pass [Ab]o[Eb]ver you
[Cm]No plague will [Bb]come upon you [Eb]
When I see the blood, I will pass [Ab]o[Eb]ver you
I will [Cm]pass o[Bb]ver [Eb]you
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Paint the doorposts, paint the lintel, stay [Ab]inside until [Eb]the dawn
Eat it standing, eat it hurried, with your [Ab]staff and your [Eb]cloak on
At [Cm]midnight came the [Bb]cry[Ab]ing all across the [Eb]land
But [Cm]the houses with the blood were [Bb]held in the LORD's own hand
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
When I see the [Eb]blood, I will pass [Ab]o[Eb]ver you
[Cm]No plague will [Bb]come upon you [Eb]
When I see the blood, I will pass [Ab]o[Eb]ver you
I will [Cm]pass o[Bb]ver [Eb]you
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Ab]This day shall be a day of [Bb]remembrance for you
And you [Cm]shall keep it as a festival to the [Bb]LORD
Throughout your gener[Eb]ations
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
When I see the blood
I will pass [Ab]o[Eb]ver you
{end_of_verse}

